{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Before they understand</b> — Rav Hai of blessed memory said: that יבינו is like קשות. And in the words of the Sages of Israel: אביונות. And the meaning is: before the thorns mature, he returns [as] a bramble; HaShem will uproot them from their place." "<b>And the meaning of חי</b> — when they are in the vitality of life, that they are moist." "<b>Like חרון</b> — like a man who storms the tree from its place in wrath. And some say: before the discerning understand that your thorns — which are small thorns — will grow and turn, like a bramble, which are large; just as the living [tree] does in the heat of his anger, so HaShem will storm them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {0 "The Hebrew here is textually difficult. 'גמילת פרח העץ' is opaque, possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally. 'אביונות' appears to be a fragmentary or technical term left as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:12.597299691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}